pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% `output DERIVABLE` claims every model of the input is a model of the output,
% and `check_file` establishes that by matching the output against the CORE
% set -- sound only while every core constraint is input-entailed.
%
% The guard covered `sol`/`soli`/`solx` logging and `soli`/`obji` objective
% bounding. It did not cover `red`/`dom`, which store a constraint that is
% satisfiability-preserving but NOT input-entailed by a licence having nothing
% to do with solutions. This proof needs neither a solution nor an objective:
%
%   x1=0, x2=1 satisfies the input `x1 + x2 >= 1`
%              and falsifies the output's `x1 >= 1`.
%
% Before the guard was widened this certified `s VERIFIED OUTPUT DERIVABLE` at
% exit 0. Same failure mode as defects 15 and 20, at the third route their
% fixes did not reach.
f 1;
red 1 x1 >= 1 : x1 1;
core id -1;
output DERIVABLE FILE;
conclusion NONE;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
